<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Castile, Castilian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of Castile was a Christian kingdom of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> and the leading power of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a>. It fought both the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a>, notably at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-navas-de-tolosa">Las Navas de Tolosa</a> in 1212. United dynastically with Aragon through Isabella and Ferdinand, Castile sponsored the voyages that founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>, while its rivalry with Portugal shaped the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Castile" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: drini · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Castile.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
